Daimon::genesis (one-tx "summon + bind" — createAccount carries genesis mandates)
├── given a createAccount carrying one genesis mandate
│   └── when the account is summoned
│       └── it should deploy at the mandate-committed address and bind the mandate (no separate bind tx)
└── given a genesis-bound recipient-lock swap mandate
    ├── when the session key direct-executes (USE) a swap routed to the allowlisted recipient
    │   └── it should execute and deliver output (no BIND payload, no ROOT sig on first use)
    └── when the session key direct-executes (USE) a swap routed to an attacker
        └── it should revert with UnauthorizedExecution (sigil contains it, same bounds as a post-deploy bind)
